    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Josh Naylor** (77.76) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92). Both benefit immensely from a favorable encounter with Zach Littell and Tatsuya Imai, respectively; their high efficiency scores are driven by a combination of pitcher vulnerability and favorable batting order placement. **Corbin Carroll** (71.85) remains a cornerstone, providing the rare combination of high-floor production and elite speed\u2014a critical factor for our internal scoring model given the scarcity of stolen bases in this 5x5 format. While **Corbin Carroll** faces a decent arm in Nick Lodolo, his dynamic platoon splits and premium order slot as the #2 hitter keep him as an essential top-tier start.\n\nThe benching of **Brice Turang** (49.77) serves as the most difficult decision of the morning. While **Brice Turang** carries substantial value for his speed, he fell just short of the efficiency threshold required to displace the current middle infield core. The optimizer favored **Travis Bazzana** (52.50) due to a superior platoon advantage against Flaherty, which effectively squeezed **Brice Turang** out of the starting nine. Meanwhile, **Max Muncy**, **Kyle Karros**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Seiya Suzuki** require monitoring as their lineup statuses are currently pending. Should these official lineups deviate significantly from our projections\u2014specifically moving **Max Muncy** or **Seiya Suzuki** down the order\u2014we will need to reassess their sub-55 scores. Risks remain moderate, primarily tied to the potential for late-scratches, but the lineup as constructed prioritizes offensive stability against pitching staffs that have shown susceptibility to high-xwOBA contact throughout the 2026 campaign.",
